<%# THE DEVOPS SIDEBAR BODY — a BROADCAST SLOT (#devops-sidebar-detail). It holds the
    sidebar's two cards, the detail (tasks/_devops_detail) and the six stage averages
    (tasks/_release_duration_card), and DeploymentsBroadcaster.devops_card replaces it
    in the same push as #devops-summary-card, both rendered from one Devops::Snapshot.
    So the card and the open sidebar can never disagree after a phase change.

    Every render must carry the id (a replace that dropped it would land once and
    never again) and no inline script (the broadcast render has no request nonce).
    space-y-4 here, not on the sidebar body: the body's spacing reaches only its
    direct children, and this wrapper is now that child.

    Locals: flow (Release::Flow or nil), wip_count, wip_by_stage, dashboard (the stage
            averages hash or nil) %>
<div id="devops-sidebar-detail" class="space-y-4" data-test="devops-sidebar-detail">
  <%= render "tasks/devops_detail", flow: local_assigns[:flow], wip_count: local_assigns[:wip_count],
             wip_by_stage: local_assigns[:wip_by_stage] %>
  <%= render "tasks/release_duration_card", dashboard: local_assigns[:dashboard],
             wip_count: local_assigns[:wip_count], card_class: "min-w-0" %>
</div>
